Original commit body from aad393cb07e6532f2dc26968eaa2c3dee6ee2cfd:

Ruby resolved `Klass.new` to `Klass#initialize` and emitted `calls`, while the
eight other analyzers that emit construction edges (dart, csharp, java, py,
js_ts, php, cpp, verilog) emitted `instantiates`. A consumer asking for object
creation by edge_type therefore omitted all of Ruby silently, and a linker held
`frozenset({"calls", "instantiates"})` to paper over the split. Ruby now emits
`instantiates`.

The dst is deliberately UNCHANGED at the initializer symbol. WI-fagit
independently converged csharp onto that same choice (PR #689): anchoring on
the class conflates "referenced as a type" with "instantiated" and breaks
reverse-slice. `evidence_type` likewise stays `ast_call` — evidence_type is the
inference PATHWAY (ADR-0028), Ruby has no `new` operator, and `ast_new` would
claim 0.95 confidence for a construct the language does not have.

Making that change safe required first fixing a defect it exposed. The
dead-code BFS keyed on `{calls, dispatches_to, wraps}`, so construction edges
carried no reachability at all. Measured directly against `_bfs_reachable`: on
`main -[instantiates]-> init -[calls]-> polish` with seeds={main}, the walk
reaches ONLY `main` — the constructor AND everything transitively downstream of
it were false dead code, for all nine emitting languages. The set now derives
its call-family half from the registry (INV-lalad), the third consumer to stop
keeping a private copy that omitted `instantiates` after taint and
verify-claims. Local extras are unioned, never substituted: `dispatches_to` and
`wraps` confer reachability but are not call constructs.

There was a fourth copy, in the test written to prevent exactly this. The
constant was a `cmd_dead_code_maybe` local, hence unimportable, so its closure
gate kept its own literal at module scope and pinned the two together by
scraping the function's source text. A drift DETECTOR is strictly weaker than
making the drift impossible: the constant is hoisted to module scope as
`Final[frozenset[str]]` and consumers import the object. The gate now asserts
what the scrape never could — that the set is RIGHT, naming each guarded
dispatch family's edge type, with `call_family_edge_types()` as a subset rather
than an equality so a future family can extend it without a spurious failure.

Also corrects the prose the widening falsified: `py.py` and
`test_closure_factory_edges.py` both stated the BFS "only follows
`{calls, dispatches_to, wraps}`".

9747 passed, 100% coverage, all six packages green in isolation, mypy ratchet
clean.

